{
  "description": "Hand-built PORT-API-OPTION cases with invented names, read by the importer's suite (packages/tools/tests/test_port_api_option_import.py) and by the input/output oracle comparator's, so the two restatements of one predicate cannot drift. {component} is the component's path. A port's fate: kept; kept-with-desc-line (kept, with a descriptive report line under DESC); skipped (a PR port); no-interface (a P- or R-port stating no interface, which the mapper skips); duplicate (a second port of one name). A verdict: the first reason that holds -- attribute, no-reference, names-no-port, wrong-dest, unkept, second, child, flag, or off (both features off, exactly the three children, on a kept port: a line too since 2026-10-07, no text of the standard giving an absent option a default) -- with its key: anchor (the PORT-REF's text as written) or shared ({behaviour}/PORT-API-OPTIONS).",
